{
  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_027 vs config_012) yielded a ~7-point accuracy gain (0.635→0.706) with all other settings held constant, making scvi_n200 the clear best RNA encoder. The image encoder dimension (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) is completely untested across all 4 experiments. Config_035 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable test that changes only the image encoder from the best configuration (config_027). This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-potential-impact axis remaining: a different backbone architecture could shift accuracy substantially in either direction. With 5 experiments left, resolving whether resnet50 or imagenet_vit_l pairs better with scvi_n200 is critical before committing remaining budget to fine-tuning aggregation/fusion choices. If resnet50 matches or beats imagenet_vit_l, it opens a new promising branch; if not, we can confidently exploit the imagenet_vit_l + scvi_n200 combination in subsequent experiments."
}

